  "query_preview": "(Monday through Thursday)...\nHigh pressure centered over the central and southern Rockies and \nplains will slowly weaken through Tuesday, then begin to \nstrengthen on Wednesday and move westward with the center near Las\nVegas for late next week. \n\nThe gradual cooling and drying trend will continue through\nWednesday with Wednesday high temperatures around 5 degrees above\naverage. High temperatures on Wednesday will range from the mid\n70s to around 80 near the coast to the mid 90s to 102 for the \nInland Empire with 108 to 112 for the lower deserts. This will be\nfollowed by a warming trend through the end of July into the first\nweekend in August.",
